Package: datakit
Title: Data Preparation Keeping Stata's Labels and Missing Values
Version: 3.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Bearak", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jbearak@guttmacher.org")
Description: Data preparation built on dtaparser. d[i, name, by = g] :=
    value makes and changes a column of a data frame or tibble, as
    generate, replace and bysort do, under R's rules. read_fixed_width()
    reads fixed-width text, such as the National Survey of Family Growth
    files, through its SAS setup file. read_parquet() and save_parquet()
    read and write Parquet files that keep value labels, variable labels
    and the extended missing values .a to .z, and return the types
    read_dta() returns.
